menu "ESP Thread Border Router settings"

    config ESP_BR_SETTINGS
        bool "Persistent border router settings, status and backup/restore"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_BORDER_ROUTER && OPENTHREAD_FTD
        default n
        help
            Adds persisted (NVS) overrides for radio, link, TREL, Thread routing, border routing,
            Backbone Router and logging settings, a radio/link status view and a JSON backup and
            restore of the Active Operational Dataset and these settings. Exposed as a REST API
            below /br/ and as Settings and Radio pages in the border router Web UI.

    config ESP_BR_SETTINGS_TREL_DEFAULT
        bool "Enable TREL when no saved setting exists"
        depends on ESP_BR_SETTINGS && OPENTHREAD_RADIO_TREL
        default y
        help
            TREL (Thread Radio Encapsulation Link) carries Thread frames over the Ethernet/Wi-Fi
            backbone, so border routers on the same LAN stay connected even when they cannot
            hear each other over IEEE 802.15.4. The saved setting overrides this default.

endmenu
